Every diagnostic layer is clean. The live lab actively contradicts the helpdesk report: host_1_1_1_1 currently reaches all four web servers via both ICMP (0% loss) and HTTP (200 OK, ~5 ms), DNS resolves correctly through the shared name server, and OSPF routing is fully converged. There is no link fault, no routing gap, no service failure, and no resource contention that could explain a complete data-centre blackout.

=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The user on host_1_1_1_1 reported a complete loss of access to the data-centre segment (web_server_0–3, dns_server), suggesting the uplink between their building and the core had failed. A thorough, multi-layer diagnostic found no supporting evidence for this claim.

**Affected component:** None — all subsystems are healthy.

**Mechanism:** A complete ICMP reachability sweep showed host_1_1_1_1 reaching the data-centre (10.200.0.x) with 0% packet loss. The OSPF control plane across all six FRR routers (router_core_1/2/3, switch_dist_1_1/2_1, switch_server_access) is fully converged: every router holds Full adjacencies, carries 10 OSPF routes, and all FRR daemons respond on both vtysh and control sockets. No interface is down or detached; no ACL or iptables rule blocks any protocol; no traffic-control shaper is applied to any interface; there are no duplicate MACs or addressing conflicts; and no device shows resource pressure or stress-tool activity. At the service layer, host_1_1_1_1 successfully resolves all four published hostnames (web0–3.local) via the shared DNS server (10.200.0.2) and receives HTTP 200 responses from all four web servers with sub-10 ms latency.

**Localization:** No device is implicated.

**Root cause:** There is no active or residual fault; the reported connectivity loss is not reproducible against the current lab state and leaves no diagnostic trace.

**Fix:** No corrective action is required. If the user experienced a genuine transient outage, it has since self-resolved; monitoring for future recurrence is advisable.
=== END ===